# E2E Testing (Playwright)

## Structure

```
e2e/
├── fixtures.ts                    # loginAs, zulipApi, authenticated (+ mock)
├── helpers/
│   ├── zulip-api-mock.ts          # page.route mock for /api/v1/**
│   ├── workspace-api-mock.ts      # page.route mock for /workspace/v1/**
│   ├── seed-auth.ts               # localStorage instance seed
│   ├── seed-chat-list-cache.ts    # IndexedDB sidebar cache seed
│   ├── network.ts                 # setBrowserOffline/Online
│   └── live-auth-env.ts           # TEST_USER_* from .env
├── mocks/
│   ├── zulip-default-responses.ts # default Zulip JSON bodies
│   └── workspace-default-responses.ts # default Workspace JSON bodies
├── pages/
│   └── connection-banner.page.ts
├── connection-resilience.spec.ts  # @mock — network/API failures
├── live/                          # @live — real Zulip (skipped without secrets)
│   ├── live-auth.spec.ts
│   └── feed-forward-live.spec.ts
└── results/                       # gitignored
```

Config: `playwright.config.ts` (root).

## Commands

```bash
npm run e2e                              # All tests (headless)
npm run e2e -- --project=chromium        # Chromium only
npm run e2e -- --grep @mock              # Resilience / mock API only
npm run e2e -- --grep-invert @live       # CI default (no live server)
npm run e2e:headed
npm run e2e:ui
npm run e2e:report
```

## Fixtures

```typescript
import { test, expect } from "./fixtures";

test("mocked shell", async ({ authenticated, zulipApi }) => {
  await expect(authenticated.locator("[data-focus-zone='topbar']")).toBeVisible();
  zulipApi.abortMatching(/\/events/, 1);
});

test("live login", async ({ page, loginAs }) => {
  test.describe.configure({ tag: "@live" });
  await loginAs(email, password, realm);
});
```

| Fixture | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `zulipApi` | `ZulipApiMock` — intercepts `**/api/v1/**` |
| (auto) | `WorkspaceApiMock` — intercepts `**/*workspace*/**` on every `page` |
| `authenticated` | Seeds auth + opens shell (uses mock) |
| `loginAs` | Real login form (live tests) |

## ZulipApiMock

```typescript
zulipApi.statusMatching(/\/api\/v1\//, 503, 10);
zulipApi.abortMatching(/\/events/, 2);
zulipApi.setNextEventsResponse({ result: "error", code: "BAD_EVENT_QUEUE_ID" });
zulipApi.restoreDefaults();
expect(zulipApi.getRegisterCallCount()).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);
```

Long-poll `/events` returns immediately with `{ result: "success", events: [] }` by default.

## Locators (priority)

1. `getByRole` / `getByLabel`
2. `getByText` (locale-aware regex: `/Перезагрузить|Reload/`)
3. `getByTestId("connection-banner")`
4. Avoid brittle CSS classes

## Tags

- `@mock` — uses `ZulipApiMock`, no real Zulip server
- `@live` — requires `TEST_USER_ZULIP_SERVER`, `TEST_USER_EMAIL`, `TEST_USER_PASSWORD`

CI runs `npm run e2e -- --project=chromium --grep-invert @live`.

## CI

GitHub Actions job `e2e` (after `check`) and GitLab `e2e-web` stage.
Artifacts: `e2e/results` on failure.

## For AI Agent

1. Prefer `authenticated` + `zulipApi` for app shell tests
2. Add resilience scenarios to `connection-resilience.spec.ts`
3. Do not add live tests without `@live` + `test.skip` for missing env
4. Never rely on real long-poll timeouts in E2E
